#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Step 1: Map classical inputs to a quantum problem {#step-1-map-classical-"
"inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"
msgstr ""
"Langkah 1: Petakan input klasik kepada masalah kuantum {#step-1-map-"
"classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Generate TFIM graph {#generate-tfim-graph}"
msgstr "Jana graf TFIM {#generate-tfim-graph}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We begin by defining the lattice of spins and the couplings between them. In"
" this tutorial, the lattice is constructed from connected triangles arranged"
" in a linear chain. Each triangle consists of three nodes connected in a "
"closed loop, and the chain is formed by linking one node of each triangle to"
" the previous triangle.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita mulakan dengan mentakrifkan kekisi spin dan gandingan antara spin-spin "
"tersebut. Dalam tutorial ini, kekisi dibina daripada segitiga yang "
"bersambung dan disusun dalam rantai linear. Setiap segitiga terdiri daripada"
" tiga nod yang bersambung dalam gelung tertutup, dan rantai dibentuk dengan "
"menghubungkan satu nod setiap segitiga kepada segitiga sebelumnya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The helper function `connected_triangles_adj_matrix` builds the adjacency "
"matrix for this structure. For a chain of $n$ triangles, the resulting graph"
" contains $2n+1$ nodes.\n"
msgstr ""
"Fungsi pembantu `connected_triangles_adj_matrix` membina matriks "
"ketetanggaan bagi struktur ini. Untuk rantai $n$ segitiga, graf yang "
"terhasil mengandungi $2n+1$ nod.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To visualize the lattice we just defined, we can plot the chain of connected"
" triangles and label each node. The function below builds the graph for a "
"chosen number of triangles and displays it.\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk menggambarkan kekisi yang baru kita takrifkan, kita boleh plot rantai "
"segitiga bersambung dan label setiap nod. Fungsi di bawah membina graf untuk"
" bilangan segitiga yang dipilih dan memaparkannya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "For this tutorial we will use a chain of 20 triangles.\n"
msgstr "Untuk tutorial ini kita akan menggunakan rantai 20 segitiga.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/transverse-field-"
"ising-model/extracted-outputs/861ab6e3-0.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/transverse-field-"
"ising-model/extracted-outputs/861ab6e3-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Coloring graph edges {#coloring-graph-edges}"
msgstr "Mewarnakan tepi graf {#coloring-graph-edges}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To implement the spin–spin coupling, it is useful to group edges that do not"
" overlap. This allows us to apply two-qubit gates in parallel. We can do "
"this with a simple edge-coloring procedure [\\[1\\]](#references), which "
"assigns a color to each edge so that edges meeting at the same node are "
"placed in different groups.\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk melaksanakan gandingan spin–spin, adalah berguna untuk mengumpulkan "
"tepi yang tidak bertindih. Ini membolehkan kita menerapkan gate dua qubit "
"secara selari. Kita boleh melakukan ini dengan prosedur pewarnaan tepi yang "
"ringkas [\\[1\\]](#references), yang menetapkan warna kepada setiap tepi "
"supaya tepi yang bertemu pada nod yang sama diletakkan dalam kumpulan "
"berbeza.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Step 2: Optimize problem for quantum hardware execution {#step-2-optimize-"
"problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"
msgstr ""
"Langkah 2: Optimumkan masalah untuk pelaksanaan perkakasan kuantum "
"{#step-2-optimize-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Generate Trotterized circuits on spin graphs {#generate-trotterized-"
"circuits-on-spin-graphs}"
msgstr ""
"Jana Circuit Trotter pada graf spin {#generate-trotterized-circuits-on-spin-"
"graphs}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To simulate the dynamics of the TFIM, we construct circuits that approximate"
" the time evolution operator.\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk mensimulasi dinamik TFIM, kita membina Circuit yang menganggar "
"operator evolusi masa.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U(t) = e^{-i H t}, \\quad \\text{where} \\quad H = -J \\sum_{\\langle i,j \\rangle} Z_i Z_j - h \\sum_i X_i .\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U(t) = e^{-i H t}, \\quad \\text{where} \\quad H = -J \\sum_{\\langle i,j \\rangle} Z_i Z_j - h \\sum_i X_i .\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "We use a second-order Trotter decomposition:\n"
msgstr "Kita menggunakan penguraian Trotter peringkat kedua:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"e^{-i H \\Delta t} \\approx e^{-i H_X \\Delta t / 2}\\, e^{-i H_Z \\Delta t}\\, e^{-i H_X \\Delta t / 2},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"e^{-i H \\Delta t} \\approx e^{-i H_X \\Delta t / 2}\\, e^{-i H_Z \\Delta t}\\, e^{-i H_X \\Delta t / 2},\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where $H_X = -h \\sum_i X_i$ and $H_Z = -J \\sum_{\\langle i,j \\rangle} Z_i"
" Z_j$.\n"
msgstr ""
"di mana $H_X = -h \\sum_i X_i$ dan $H_Z = -J \\sum_{\\langle i,j \\rangle} "
"Z_i Z_j$.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The $H_X$ term is implemented with layers of `RX` rotations.\n"
msgstr "Sebutan $H_X$ dilaksanakan dengan lapisan putaran `RX`.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The $H_Z$ term is implemented with layers of `RZZ` gates along the edges of "
"the interaction graph.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sebutan $H_Z$ dilaksanakan dengan lapisan gate `RZZ` sepanjang tepi graf "
"interaksi.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The angles of these gates are determined by the transverse field $h$, the "
"coupling constant $J$, and the time step $\\Delta t$. By stacking multiple "
"Trotter steps, we generate circuits of increasing depth that approximate the"
" system's dynamics. The functions `generate_tfim_circ_custom_graph` and "
"`trotter_circuits` construct a Trotterized quantum circuit from an arbitrary"
" spin interaction graph.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sudut gate-gate ini ditentukan oleh medan melintang $h$, pemalar gandingan "
"$J$, dan langkah masa $\\Delta t$. Dengan menindih beberapa langkah Trotter,"
" kita menjana Circuit dengan kedalaman yang semakin meningkat bagi "
"menganggar dinamik sistem. Fungsi `generate_tfim_circ_custom_graph` dan "
"`trotter_circuits` membina Circuit kuantum Trotter daripada graf interaksi "
"spin sewenang-wenangnya.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Estimate single-qubit magnetizations $\\langle Z_i \\rangle$ {#estimate-"
"single-qubit-magnetizations-langle-z-i-rangle}"
msgstr ""
"Anggar kemagnetan qubit tunggal $\\langle Z_i \\rangle$ {#estimate-single-"
"qubit-magnetizations-langle-z-i-rangle}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To study the dynamics of the model, we want to measure the magnetization of "
"each qubit, defined by the expectation value $\\langle Z_i \\rangle = "
"\\langle \\psi | Z_i | \\psi \\rangle$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk mengkaji dinamik model, kita ingin mengukur kemagnetan setiap qubit, "
"yang ditakrifkan oleh nilai jangkaan $\\langle Z_i \\rangle = \\langle \\psi"
" | Z_i | \\psi \\rangle$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In simulations, we can compute this directly from the measurement outcomes. "
"The function `z_expectation` processes the bitstring counts and returns the "
"value of $\\langle Z_i \\rangle$ for a chosen qubit index. On real hardware,"
" we evaluate the same quantity by specifying the Pauli operator using the "
"function `generate_z_observables`, and then the backend computes the "
"expectation value.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam simulasi, kita boleh mengira ini terus daripada hasil pengukuran. "
"Fungsi `z_expectation` memproses kiraan bitstring dan mengembalikan nilai "
"$\\langle Z_i \\rangle$ bagi indeks qubit yang dipilih. Pada perkakasan "
"sebenar, kita menilai kuantiti yang sama dengan menentukan operator Pauli "
"menggunakan fungsi `generate_z_observables`, kemudian Backend mengira nilai "
"jangkaan tersebut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We now define the parameters for generating the Trotterized circuits. In "
"this tutorial, the lattice is a chain of 20 connected triangles, which "
"corresponds to a 41-qubit system.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita kini takrifkan parameter untuk menjana Circuit Trotter. Dalam tutorial "
"ini, kekisi ialah rantai 20 segitiga bersambung, yang bersamaan sistem "
"41-Qubit.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Step 3: Execute using Qiskit primitives {#step-3-execute-using-qiskit-"
"primitives}"
msgstr ""
"Langkah 3: Laksanakan menggunakan primitif Qiskit {#step-3-execute-using-"
"qiskit-primitives}"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Run MPS simulation {#run-mps-simulation}"
msgstr "Jalankan simulasi MPS {#run-mps-simulation}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The list of Trotterized circuits is executed using the "
"`matrix_product_state` simulator with an arbitrary choice of $4096$ shots. "
"The MPS method provides an efficient approximation of the circuit dynamics, "
"with accuracy determined by the chosen bond dimension. For the system sizes "
"considered here, the default bond dimension is sufficient to capture the "
"magnetization dynamics with high fidelity. The raw counts are normalized, "
"and from these we compute the single-qubit expectation values $\\langle Z_i "
"\\rangle$ at each Trotter step. Finally, we calculate the average over all "
"qubits to obtain a single curve that shows how the magnetization changes "
"over time.\n"
msgstr ""
"Senarai Circuit Trotter dilaksanakan menggunakan simulator "
"`matrix_product_state` dengan pilihan sewenang-wenang sebanyak $4096$ "
"tembakan. Kaedah MPS memberikan anggaran cekap bagi dinamik Circuit, dengan "
"ketepatan yang ditentukan oleh dimensi ikatan yang dipilih. Bagi saiz sistem"
" yang dipertimbangkan di sini, dimensi ikatan lalai sudah cukup untuk "
"menangkap dinamik kemagnetan dengan ketepatan tinggi. Kiraan mentah "
"dinormalkan, dan daripada situ kita mengira nilai jangkaan qubit tunggal "
"$\\langle Z_i \\rangle$ pada setiap langkah Trotter. Akhirnya, kita mengira "
"purata ke atas semua qubit untuk mendapatkan satu lengkung tunggal yang "
"menunjukkan perubahan kemagnetan dari masa ke masa.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Run on hardware {#run-on-hardware}"
msgstr "Jalankan pada perkakasan {#run-on-hardware}"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Run on hardware with Fire Opal {#run-on-hardware-with-fire-opal}"
msgstr ""
"Jalankan pada perkakasan dengan Fire Opal {#run-on-hardware-with-fire-opal}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We evaluate the magnetization dynamics on real quantum hardware. Fire Opal "
"provides a Qiskit Function that extends the standard Qiskit Runtime "
"Estimator primitive with automated error suppression and performance "
"management. We submit the Trotterized circuits directly to an IBM&reg; "
"backend while Fire Opal handles the noise-aware execution.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita menilai dinamik kemagnetan pada perkakasan kuantum sebenar. Fire Opal "
"menyediakan Fungsi Qiskit yang melanjutkan primitif Estimator Qiskit Runtime"
" standard dengan penyekatan ralat automatik dan pengurusan prestasi. Kita "
"menghantar Circuit Trotter terus ke Backend IBM&reg; manakala Fire Opal "
"mengendalikan pelaksanaan yang peka terhadap hingar.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We prepare a list of `pubs`, where each item contains a circuit and the "
"corresponding Pauli-Z observables. These are passed to Fire Opal's estimator"
" function, which returns the expectation values $\\langle Z_i \\rangle$ for "
"each qubit at each Trotter step. The results can then be averaged over "
"qubits to obtain the magnetization curve from hardware.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita menyediakan senarai `pubs`, di mana setiap item mengandungi Circuit dan"
" pemerhatian Pauli-Z yang sepadan. Ini dihantar ke fungsi Estimator Fire "
"Opal, yang mengembalikan nilai jangkaan $\\langle Z_i \\rangle$ bagi setiap "
"qubit pada setiap langkah Trotter. Keputusan tersebut kemudiannya boleh "
"dipuratakan ke atas qubit untuk mendapatkan lengkung kemagnetan daripada "
"perkakasan.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Step 4: Post-process and return result in desired classical format "
"{#step-4-post-process-and-return-result-in-desired-classical-format}"
msgstr ""
"Langkah 4: Proses selepas dan kembalikan keputusan dalam format klasik yang "
"diingini {#step-4-post-process-and-return-result-in-desired-classical-"
"format}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Finally, we compare the magnetization curve from the simulator with the "
"results obtained on real hardware. Plotting both side by side shows how "
"closely the hardware execution with Fire Opal matches the noiseless baseline"
" across Trotter steps.\n"
msgstr ""
"Akhirnya, kita membandingkan lengkung kemagnetan daripada simulator dengan "
"keputusan yang diperoleh pada perkakasan sebenar. Memplot kedua-duanya "
"secara berdampingan menunjukkan betapa rapatnya pelaksanaan perkakasan "
"dengan Fire Opal mencocoki garis dasar tanpa hingar merentasi langkah "
"Trotter.\n"

